<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Victoriano Huerta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1850–1916</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Victoriano <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huerta">Huerta</a> was a Mexican general who seized power in February 1913 in a coup against President Francisco Madero, who was then murdered. His dictatorship faced the Constitutionalist rebellion and the hostility of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, which occupied Veracruz in 1914. Defeated, he resigned in July 1914 and died in American custody in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a> in 1916.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/victoriano-huerta.jpg" alt="Victoriano Huerta" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Victoriano_Huerta_en_1912.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
